# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# WHY: Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a Windows clone gets
# CRLF locally while the repository stores LF. That breaks exactly the things
# this repo now ships: bash hook scripts (.claude/hooks/*, scripts/hooks/*)
# fail on a CRLF shebang under git-bash, and any future byte-comparing guard
# goes red on a tree nobody edited. Ported from ally-os [FEAT-480], trimmed to
# what this repo carries.
#
# An existing Windows working copy may show a one-time renormalisation on the
# next checkout (`git add --renormalize .` if so). No effect on POSIX checkouts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types, named explicitly rather than left to detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
